\section{Experience}

\textbf{Software Engineer, DNS Team (previously SRE)} \textemdash{} Cloudflare, \textit{Jul 2015 - Jul 2026}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Domain Connect DNS Provider implementation, maintenance, and IETF
      draft RFC work.
\item Co-invented a patented approach to decoupling IP address bindings from
      their use in a distributed cloud network.
\item Made the Cloudflare's China network IP addressing and traffic
      distribution to work, being the principal engineer writing the code.
\item Developed self-healing network automation for Cloudflare's edge DNS
      infrastructure to automatically mitigate edge failures.
\item Optimized dnstap-based recursion logging, reducing analytics pipeline
      resource usage by 90\%.
\item Moved from site reliability engineering into a full-time Golang role
      on the authoritative DNS team.
\item In a SRE role for first couple years in Cloudflare; covered on-call,
      attack mitigation, release engineering, and incident resolution.
\item During SRE my job included responsibility over the servers in China as
      the subject matter expert.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Senior Systems Administrator / Infrastructure Architect} \textemdash{} Lastminute.com, \textit{Sep 2012 - Jun 2015}
\begin{itemize}
\itemsep 0em
\item Moved legacy infrastructure onto Puppet, Foreman and Pulp, and
      introduced Jenkins pipelines for developer self-service.
\item Wrote F5 Graceful Scaling (\texttt{f5gs}) helper utility to coordinate service
      availability and discovery. The tool is written in C, has native systemd
      bindings, and is using embedded programming concepts.
\item Wrote the technical plan for moving the company's data centre from the
      US to Europe, covering provisioning and configuration management,
      using GitLab and r10k.
\item Worked with distributed teams in London, India and Texas on
      monitoring, inventory, account management and orchestration, while
      maintaining PCI compliance.
\end{itemize}

